From: "Derek J. Clark" <derekjohn.clark@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 15:52:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] HID: hid-lenovo-go-s: Add kobject_uevent notify during
 reset-resume
References: bsc#1012628
Patch-mainline: 7.3.2
Git-commit: 81e8c0bb3831fb84ef44417bba1b52333d0580a9

commit 81e8c0bb3831fb84ef44417bba1b52333d0580a9 upstream.

Adds kobject_uevent notification after setting os_mode attribute on resume.

Fixes: 3524900cc571bd922a ("HID: hid-lenovo-go-s: restore OS_TYPE after resume from s2idle")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Derek J. Clark <derekjohn.clark@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Jiri Kosina <jkosina@suse.com>
Signed-off-by: Greg Kroah-Hartman <gregkh@linuxfoundation.org>
Signed-off-by: Jiri Slaby <jslaby@suse.cz>
---
 drivers/hid/hid-lenovo-go-s.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/hid/hid-lenovo-go-s.c b/drivers/hid/hid-lenovo-go-s.c
index 48cde8799309..e5c4104a3adb 100644
--- a/drivers/hid/hid-lenovo-go-s.c
+++ b/drivers/hid/hid-lenovo-go-s.c
@@ -1618,6 +1618,7 @@ static int hid_gos_cfg_reset_resume(struct hid_device *hdev)
 	if (drvdata.os_mode != os_mode)
 		return -ENODEV;
 
+	kobject_uevent(&drvdata.hdev->dev.kobj, KOBJ_CHANGE);
 	return 0;
 }
 
-- 
